== F-19 criteria, written before the change ==
C1  README.md's "Client tests" row quotes no number, matching the policy the "Backend tests" row already follows
    ("counts change as ... are added"). A count the backend suite cannot check is a count that goes stale: 198 was
    written when the suite was smaller and read 198 while it grew to 496.
C2  A backend test fails if that row quotes a count. The guard must not pass vacuously, so it also fails if the
    row is missing altogether (the positive control for an absence check).
C3  Sabotage, each restored byte-identical: putting "198 passing" back turns the guard red; deleting the row turns
    it red.
C4  The full backend suite passes. Nothing under backend/app or app/lib changes, so the scientific core does not
    move and no re-bind is needed.
