== F-20: stopped, a defect rather than a missing test ==
Research before writing any test, because a test that pins unsafe behaviour as correct is worse than no test.
Path 1 (cpic_engine.select_annotation, "candidates = matched or usable"). A constructed probe, not an observed
event: the real CYP2C19 Poor Metabolizer report fixture, with clopidogrel's guideline left holding only CPIC's real
Normal Metabolizer row (classification Strong, wording from test-data/reference/cpic_expectations.json). The real
report, untouched, gives Ineffective with "Avoid clopidogrel if possible...". The probe gives "No PGx-guided
adjustment identified", action "If considering clopidogrel, use at standard dose (75 mg/day)", label rule
standard_dosing. The only safeguard was the warning "showing the strongest available row. Treat with extra
caution."; the request-time contradiction check did not degrade it. "Strongest" ranks evidence strength, not
caution, so when the fallback fires on an asserted phenotype it can serve the reassuring row of a different
phenotype - the false-reassurance direction.
Whether it happens on real data: over the 400 cached cohort reports x 6 drugs (2,400 evaluations) the fallback fires
309 times (fluorouracil 98, simvastatin 209, clopidogrel 2), and evaluate() returns Unknown in all 309, because in
each the phenotype was not asserted and the earlier gate returned before the fallback could produce a label. S1-S6
and the A4 rows never reached it (Part A). So it is latent, not observed: on real data the protection comes from a
different layer, not from the fallback. A CPIC or PharmCAT wording change that leaves an asserted phenotype with no
matching row would reach it.
Path 2 (an Unknown result carrying a CPIC directive in action): NOT MEASURED. Reading the code, two engine
sub-paths label Unknown while still building the recommendation from the CPIC row (the fallback_unmatched rule and
the request-time contradiction downgrade), and main.py rebuilds without CPIC text only in the coverage-gate case.
The measurement that would show whether either occurs was stopped before it ran; no result exists.
No F-20 test or engine change is committed. Fixing path 1 changes backend/app/cpic_engine.py, which is in the
scientific core, so it needs its own plan, zero-regression and a re-bind, and the owner's decision.
